  "description": "The 2026 election for New York's 8th congressional district will be held on November 3, 2026, with a primary election on June 23, 2026. The district covers portions of central Brooklyn, including neighborhoods such as Bedford-Stuyvesant, Crown Heights, Brownsville, and East New York. Incumbent Democrat Hakeem Jeffries, the House Minority Leader, is seeking re-election and faces a Democratic primary challenge from New York City Council Member Chi Oss\u00e9, a democratic socialist, as well as a challenge from progressive activist Vance Bostic. The district is overwhelmingly Democratic and is rated \"Safe D\" by major nonpartisan forecasters, making the Democratic primary the de facto competitive contest in this cycle.",
